3771:LOGBOOK.md:852:- COVERAGE: Swift `perform` tests now inject invalid/throwing writes, throwing reads, and EOF, assert stable code/phase mappings, and prove cancel/reset/close cleanup. Full validation passes: `make relay-protocol-check` (19 selected protocol tests), `swift test` (129/129), Go vet/test with `CGO_ENABLED=0` and 92.6% statement coverage, strict Swift format, gofmt, core-boundary check, `git diff --check`, and board validation.
3776:LOGBOOK.md:911:- VERIFICATION: Reviewer reran independently on the exact tree: `make validate-native` exit 0 (iOS device/sim + macOS provider/harness matrix, 110 Swift tests), `make validate-core` exit 0, `make validate-libssh2` real rekey/KEX exit 0. `otool -l` confirmed every slice: HEV ios/tvos minos 18.0, macos 15.0; ReluxLibSSH2 ios 18.0, macos 15.0 — no 10.14/11.0 records remain.
3781:LOGBOOK.md:950:- ROOT CAUSE: `HEVDescriptorBorrowHandle.waitForReturn()` joins HEV and only then calls `runtime.statistics()` (`Sources/ReluxTunnelNativeAdapter/HEVIntegration.swift:409-423`). Pinned unmodified HEV calls `hev_socks5_tunnel_fini()` before `hev_socks5_tunnel_main_from_str()` returns, and that fini resets all four `stat_tx_*`/`stat_rx_*` globals to zero (`src/hev-socks5-tunnel.c:657-671`). The public stats call after join therefore cannot observe completed-run traffic.
3782:LOGBOOK.md:951:- EVIDENCE: `swift test --filter realHEVTCPMatrix` reaches the real SOCKS fixture and validates the full stream lifecycle, then fails only the `hev_transmitted_packets > 0` and `hev_received_packets > 0` assertions. Log: `.temp/TASK-260715-35wctc/swift-test-tcp-01.log`.
3784:LOGBOOK.md:973:- ROUTING: This is the third fork-gap round anticipated by TASK-260720-2sltje. Do not add a partial/mock-only adapter. Recommend failing libssh2 red at M0 unless its value justifies one explicitly approved consolidated fork extension for manual windows, typed open failures, and lossless exec-exit metadata; the alternative is an explicit M0-to-M3/common-contract revision. Exact evidence and resume decision are attached as `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_third-public-api-blocker.md`.
3799:LOGBOOK.md:1025:- BLOCKER: Native Darwin arm64 and Rosetta Darwin amd64 identity+stdio clean-exit checks pass as unprivileged UID 502. Native Intel macOS, Linux amd64, and Linux arm64 remain unexecuted. Exact-commit GitHub Actions run `29855573312` never started any job because GitHub rejected the account billing/spending state. No approved Linux emulator or native Intel fixture is available locally.
3804:LOGBOOK.md:1035:- FINDING: During any KEX (client- or server-initiated) upstream's state machine rejects outbound `channelData` with `protocolViolation` (`SSHConnectionStateMachine.swift:1060-1076`), failing the child write promise. Pre-existing upstream behavior, unchanged by the fork — but automatic byte/time rekey makes the collision window likely under bulk traffic. The NIOSSH adapter (TASK-260715-1af33i) MUST gate/queue child writes on `rekeySnapshot.keyExchangeInProgress` / `NIOSSHRekeyStartedEvent`→`NIOSSHRekeySucceededEvent`; the fork exposes exactly this observability for the contract's "writes MAY suspend" clause.
