24722:### 2313 — UDP teardown snapshot gate passes twenty consecutive full runs (BUG-260728-2j25tu)
24723:- VERIFICATION: A fresh reset-on-any-failure streak passed 20/20 consecutive unfiltered `swift test` runs on the final tree. Every invocation exited 0, passed 427 tests in 35 suites, and recorded passes for both `relayLifecycleOutcomes` and `staleGenerationTerminalCallbacks`. Task-scoped logs are retained under `.temp/BUG-260728-2j25tu/full-runs/`.
24724:- AUDIT: Every adapter-internal snapshot following peer EOF in `HEVUDPDatagramAdapterTests` awaits `waitForPendingTeardowns`; the only nearby snapshot without the seam is `RecordingUDPRelay.snapshot()`, which is relay-fixture state rather than adapter-internal teardown state. The barrier begins before channel close publishes EOF and completes after connection accounting plus any local registry cleanup, without sleep, retry, eventually polling, or cancellation/generation semantic changes.
24725:- VALIDATION: Recursive Swift format lint, `swift build`, and `git diff --check` exit 0. `task-board validate` also exits 0 while reporting the known parent aggregate anomaly: `STORY-260715-1nsw9p` is stored as `to-dev` while this child is `development`; the developer handoff is expected to recompute the story aggregate.
24727:### 2245 — Rekey/open deadline coverage uses the injected clock (BUG-260811-3qdo3e)
24730:- VERIFICATION: The exact rekey/open case passes after the change, and the five cancellation/rekey/automatic-keepalive/channel-pressure regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A fresh reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and exit 0, including prior failure positions 3, 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, strict recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The pre/post sshd listener set remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815, and TASK-260715-1u2vpc's approved algorithm matrix remains present.
24732:### 2225 — Keepalive aggregate coverage synchronizes on emitted events (BUG-260811-3qdo3e)
24733:- ROOT CAUSE: A fresh post-review aggregate gate reproduced one final in-scope test race at the historical run-13 position. `automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey` used at most 500 scheduler yields before reading each `keepalivesSent` counter. Under aggregate load, the automatic task had not emitted `.keepaliveSent` before either assertion, even though the fatal keepalive self-join was fixed and the suite exited normally. Fixed yield counts are not a synchronization boundary.
24734:- IMPLEMENTATION: `SuspendingRekeyObserver` now counts production `.keepaliveSent` events and resumes continuation-backed threshold waiters. The positive long-rekey test awaits the first and second emitted events before asserting the corresponding transport counters. Manual-clock advancement, rekey suspension, scoped cancellation, no implicit idle timeout, fatal teardown ownership, and the TASK-260715-1u2vpc algorithm matrix are unchanged; no sleep, timeout, skip, or wall-clock mask was added.
24735:- VERIFICATION: The four lifecycle regressions pass together 30/30 consecutive focused runs. A final reset-on-any-failure streak passes 20/20 unfiltered `swift test --skip-build` runs with 427 tests in 35 suites per run and 16–18 second durations, including historical runs 13, 16, and 17. `make validate-core`, `make validate-libssh2`, warning-free recursive Swift format lint, and `git diff --check` exit 0. The sshd listener set before and after remains the same older PIDs 1330 and 34815.
24736:- ANOMALY: The first fresh streak reset at run 7 with an unrelated HEV association snapshot assertion; the exact HEV case immediately passed focused. The next streak reset at run 13 with the reproduced keepalive counter race above. Both failing exit-1 logs are retained and neither run was counted toward the final streak.
24739:- REVIEW: The scoped cancellation test plus the positive and fatal automatic-keepalive regressions pass together with exit 0, and inspection accepts the no-self-join ownership fix, zero-resource assertions, and retained TASK-260715-1u2vpc algorithm matrix.
24740:- GATE: A reviewer-owned unfiltered streak passed 16 consecutive 427-test runs, including historical hang positions 13 and 16, then run 17 exited 1 because `channelOperationPressureIsBounded` observed `.cancelled` instead of `.resourceLimitExceeded`. The unchanged pressure test reproduced independently after nine focused passes; focused run 10 exited 1 with the same mismatch. The mandatory 20-run aggregate gate therefore remains failing even though the cancellation and keepalive cases passed in the failed aggregate run.
24741:- FINDING: The pressure fixture waits only for the actor-side count to reach 64 while the admitted exit operations concurrently enter network progress and failure cleanup. A waiter can begin channel disposal before the above-cap probe is admitted, causing `beginChannelOperation` to prefer the disposal code `.cancelled` over the cap error. Rework must make the cap boundary deterministic without weakening the expected error, skipping the case, or masking it with timing.
